## Appendix C: Derivation of the Reallocation Equation

### C.1 Task-Level Labor Demand

For a non-automated cognitive task $i$, cost minimization implies:
$$l_t(i) = \left(\frac{w_t}{A_{L,t}}\right)^{-\sigma} \left(\frac{c_t(i)}{P_t}\right)^{-\varepsilon} \frac{Y_t}{P_t}. \tag{C.1}$$

Under (A2), all non-automated cognitive tasks share the same unit cost $c_{\text{non-auto},t}$. Aggregating over the mass $1 - \mathcal{A}_{C,t}$:
$$L_{C,t} = (1 - \mathcal{A}_{C,t}) \left(\frac{w_t}{A_{L,t}}\right)^{-\sigma} \left(\frac{c_{\text{non-auto},t}}{P_t}\right)^{-\varepsilon} \frac{Y_t}{P_t}. \tag{C.2}$$

### C.2 Log-Linearization

Take logs:
$$\ln L_{C,t} = \ln(1 - \mathcal{A}_{C,t}) - \sigma(\ln w_t - \ln A_{L,t}) - \varepsilon(\ln c_{\text{non-auto},t} - \ln P_t) + \ln Y_t - \ln P_t. \tag{C.3}$$

Differentiate:
$$\hat{L}_{C,t} = -\frac{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}}{1 - \mathcal{A}_{C,t}} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} - \sigma(\hat{w}_t - \hat{A}_{L,t}) - \varepsilon(\hat{c}_{\text{non-auto},t} - \hat{P}_t) + \hat{Y}_t - \hat{P}_t. \tag{C.4}$$

Under the maintained assumption that the relative price term is constant at the margin $(\hat{c}_{\text{non-auto},t} = \hat{P}_t)$, this simplifies to:
$$\hat{L}_{C,t} = \hat{Y}_t - \sigma(\hat{w}_t - \hat{A}_{L,t}) - \varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}}, \tag{C.5}$$
where
$$\varsigma_{C,t} = \frac{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}}{1 - \mathcal{A}_{C,t}}. \tag{C.6}$$

### C.3 Fixed Labor Supply

Labor supply is fixed: $L_{C,t} + L_{I,t} = \bar{L}$, so:
$$dL_{C,t} = -dL_{I,t}. \tag{C.7}$$

Therefore:
$$\Delta L_{I,t} = -\Delta L_{C,t} = -L_{C,t-1} \hat{L}_{C,t} = L_{C,t-1} \left[ \varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} + \sigma \hat{w}_t - \sigma \hat{A}_{L,t} - \hat{Y}_t \right]. \tag{C.8}$$

### C.4 Wage–Output Co-Movement

Under the maintained assumption $\hat{w}_t \approx \hat{Y}_t$:
$$\Delta L_{I,t} = L_{C,t-1} \left[ \varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} - \sigma \hat{A}_{L,t} + (\sigma - 1) \hat{Y}_t \right]. \tag{C.9}$$

This is equation (35) in the main text.

### C.5 The Two Forces

The change in interpersonal employment is driven by:

1. **Net displacement:** $\varsigma_{C,t} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} - \widehat{n_t}$.
2. **Labor released by augmentation:** $(1-\sigma) \hat{A}_{L,t}$.

When $\sigma = 0.5$, half of the time saved by AI is reinvested into the same task; the other half is released to the broader economy.

### C.6 Comparative Statics

$$\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial \mathcal{A}_{C,t}} = L_{C,t-1} \frac{\partial \varsigma_{C,t}}{\partial \mathcal{A}_{C,t}} \widehat{\mathcal{A}_{C,t}} > 0, \tag{C.10}$$
since $\varsigma_{C,t}$ is increasing in $\mathcal{A}_{C,t}$.

$$\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial n_t} = -L_{C,t-1} \frac{\partial \widehat{n_t}}{\partial n_t} < 0. \tag{C.11}$$

$$\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial A_{L,t}} = -L_{C,t-1} \sigma < 0. \tag{C.12}$$

$$\frac{\partial \Delta L_{I,t}}{\partial \sigma} = L_{C,t-1} \left[ -\hat{A}_{L,t} + \hat{Y}_t \right] < 0 \quad \text{if} \quad \hat{A}_{L,t} > \hat{Y}_t. \tag{C.13}$$

