## Appendix G: Static Directed Technical Change

### G.1 The Innovator's Problem

A representative innovator chooses $z_t \in [0,1]$ to maximize:
$$\max_{z_t} \ \Pi_t = \pi_N z_t \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} + \pi_A (1 - z_t) \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta}. \tag{G.1}$$

### G.2 First-Order Condition

$$\frac{\partial \Pi_t}{\partial z_t} = \pi_N \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} - \pi_A \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta} = 0. \tag{G.2}$$

### G.3 Solution

Rearranging:
$$\pi_N \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} = \pi_A \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta}. \tag{G.3}$$

Dividing both sides by $\pi_A (w_t/r_t)^{\eta}$:
$$\frac{\pi_N}{\pi_A} = \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}. \tag{G.4}$$

Solving for $z_t^*$:
$$z_t^* = \frac{1}{1 + \frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}}. \tag{G.5}$$

### G.4 Comparative Statics

$$\frac{\partial z_t^*}{\partial (w_t/r_t)} = \frac{\frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} 2\eta \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta-1} \frac{1}{w_t/r_t}}{\left[1 + \frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}\right]^2} > 0. \tag{G.6}$$

$$\frac{\partial z_t^*}{\partial (\pi_N/\pi_A)} = \frac{\left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}}{\left[1 + \frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}\right]^2} \cdot \frac{1}{\pi_A/\pi_N} > 0. \tag{G.7}$$

$$\frac{\partial z_t^*}{\partial \eta} = -\frac{\frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta} \ln\left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right) \cdot 2}{\left[1 + \frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}\right]^2} \gtrless 0. \tag{G.8}$$

### G.5 Reinstatement

The mass of new labor-intensive tasks is:
$$n_t = \bar{n} + \nu z_t^* \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} = \bar{n} + \frac{\nu \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta}}{1 + \frac{\pi_A}{\pi_N} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{2\eta}}. \tag{G.9}$$

This is bounded in $[\bar{n}, \bar{n} + \nu]$ and nests the reduced-form specification as $\pi_A/\pi_N \to 0$.

### G.6 Dynamic Extension (Sketch)

A fully dynamic version would replace the static profit functions with:
$$\Pi_{N,t} = \mathbb{E}_t \sum_{s=t}^\infty \beta^{s-t} \pi_{N,s} z_s \left(\frac{w_s}{r_s}\right)^{\eta}, \tag{G.10}$$
$$\Pi_{A,t} = \mathbb{E}_t \sum_{s=t}^\infty \beta^{s-t} \pi_{A,s} (1 - z_s) \left(\frac{r_s}{w_s}\right)^{\eta}. \tag{G.11}$$

The first-order condition becomes an Euler equation:
$$\pi_{N,t} \left(\frac{w_t}{r_t}\right)^{\eta} + \beta \mathbb{E}_t \frac{\partial V_{N,t+1}}{\partial z_t} = \pi_{A,t} \left(\frac{r_t}{w_t}\right)^{\eta} + \beta \mathbb{E}_t \frac{\partial V_{A,t+1}}{\partial z_t}. \tag{G.12}$$

This is left for future research.

